 &nbsp; 
 
 
 4. 🕔 After hours: NBA&#x27;s Euro step 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The NBA is aiming to raise at least $10.9 billion to launch a new basketball league in Europe, Bloomberg reported .

 State of play: The NBA is hoping to start the European league in October 2027.

 The league is partnering with financial institutions including Apollo Global Management, Ares Management, Blackstone and JPMorgan Chase. Reality check: "13 Euroleague shareholder clubs, who already operate a Europe-wide basketball competition, rejected a formal merger with NBA Europe," Bloomberg reported.

 
 
